I implemented the node, but not the two operations requests. The node's world holds only `kb-read`. It has no filesystem (so no log file) and no `http-client` import (so no call to the metadata service). Adding either would exceed the node's declared capability scope, and I can't add a dependency. The text of the input should also not go into a URL. The output is unchanged by this.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{moderated-query, conversation-context};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: moderated-query) -> conversation-context;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(query: ModeratedQuery) -> ConversationContext {
        let q = query.query;
        let mut question = q.question;

        // Defensive: the contract guarantees <= 512 on input, keep it on output.
        if question.len() > 512 {
            let mut end = 512;
            while !question.is_char_boundary(end) {
                end -= 1;
            }
            question.truncate(end);
        }

        let knowledge = crate::aap::caps::kb_read::lookup(&question);

        ConversationContext {
            intent: q.intent,
            question,
            knowledge,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

